Machine learning is basically ability of the computer to learn without human intervention.
ML allows for automatic updation to the model , as it learns via the data , is highly flexible over traditional computing 
we do not need to add rules after every change to environment

TYPES- on training supervision

1. Supervised ML
- is given data with labels/targets so it can learn under supervision 
-training set involves desired solutions 
2. Unsupervised ML
- Training data is unlabeled
- system tries to learn without a teacher , usually by seeing patterns in the data via data mining .
-we often use dimensionality reduction to reduce excess features
-always reduce the dimensions in your training data using algorithms , allow faster loads , better results
-Clustering , anomaly detection - different and very rare like extremities
-novelty detection - new instances that are different
-association rule learning - dig and find intresting relations among attributes

3.Semi Supervised ML
-some is labeled,some not
-most are combinations of Supervised and UnSupervised

4.Self Supervised ML
-Generating a labeled dataset from a unlabeled one
-Now any supervised algorithm can be used on this
-usually have to tweak model asper needs

Reinforcement learning
-involves an agent in an unknown environment , where it observes the environment , select and performs tasks
gets rewarded (Penalty or reward) - to learn from best strategy - a POLICY
-policy defines what action it chooses for a situation

1.batch learning
-offline learning, it uses what it already knows against changing environments
-this phenomenon called data drift or model rotting , to prevent have to train a fresh new model on old + new data taking hours ,so you will likely train it like weekly or as needs
can be automated , but uses a lot of resources

2.Online learning
-train system incrementally by feeding it data sequences 
-each step is fast and cheap
-for systems that need constant changes
-learning rate - how fast it adapts to new data , more quicker leads to forgetting older data
-bad data can cause quick degredations to the model 

